// # ooda/std Standard Library Audit TLDR
//
// Logline: 8-Dimensional Red Team audit of the ooda/std standard library (6605 .oo files across 37 subdirectories). Documents the systemic Pillar 6 mod.oo seam violation, the 256-line cap compliance, the representative crypto/mod.oo fix applied, and the audit verdict for the 35 subdirectories that still lack a mod.oo entry door.
//
// Setup: This is a project documentation file at the strategic governance plane, sibling to openOODA/runtime/SUBSTRATE_AUDIT_TLDR.oot. The audit covers the entire ooda/std/ tree.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Beat 1: Audit methodology and scope.
//   2. Beat 2: 256-line cap compliance verification.
//   3. Beat 3: Pillar 6 mod.oo seam violation inventory (35/37 affected).
//   4. Beat 4: Representative first-principles fix: crypto/mod.oo created.
//   5. Beat 5: Audit verdict and path forward for the remaining 34 subdirectories.
//   6. Beat 6: Batch 1 Pillar 6 closure: 5 subdirectories closed.
//   7. Beat 7: Batch 2 Pillar 6 stub upgrades: 4 stubs upgraded.
//   8. Beat 8: Batch 3 Pillar 6 closure: 5 subdirectories closed.
//   9. Beat 9: Batch 4 Pillar 6 closure: 5 subdirectories closed.

# === Beat 1: Audit methodology ===

// The audit used the 8-Dimensional Red Team matrix (probes e1 through e8)
// per REDTEAM.oot against the ooda/std/ tree. Scope: 6605 .oo files
// across 37 first-level subdirectories plus 10 root-level .oo files.
// The audit focused on two systemic questions:
//   (1) Is the 256-line cap (per FORMAT.oot §1.3) enforced?
//   (2) Is the Pillar 6 mod.oo seam rule (per FORMAT.oot §1.4) enforced?
//
// Subdirectories surveyed: actor, ai, archive, bio, chem, cli, collections,
// compression, compile, core, crypto, data, diag, econ, encoding, fmt,
// formal_proofs, fs, hash, hw, io, markup, math, net, os, phys, principles,
// proof_verifiers, robot, sec, simd, sync, test, text, time, ui. (35 of 37
// lack mod.oo; only fmt/ and net/ have it.)

# === Beat 2: 256-line cap compliance ===

// The 256-line cap is per-FORMAT.oot §1.3 a project-wide invariant for
// .oo and .oot files. A targeted scan of the largest .oo files in
// ooda/std found:
//
//   std/simd/simd_ops_body.oo         250 lines  (within cap)
//   std/crypto/chacha20.oo            249 lines  (within cap)
//   std/crypto/sha512.oo              231 lines  (within cap)
//   std/crypto/curve25519.oo          244 lines  (within cap)
//   std/crypto/sha256_engine.oo       224 lines  (within cap)
//   std/crypto/keys_engine.oo         226 lines  (within cap)
//
// Conclusion: the .oo files in ooda/std are 256-line compliant. The cap
// invariant holds at the file level. (Earlier suspicion of > 256 lines
// was a size-based false positive -- crypto and SIMD files have very
// long single-line constants, not excess code.)

# === Beat 3: Pillar 6 mod.oo seam violation inventory ===

