# === Beat 4: Representative first-principles fix: crypto/mod.oo ===

// The crypto/ subdirectory was chosen as the most security-critical
// representative. It contains 61 .oo files implementing SHA-256/512,
// HMAC, AES, chacha20, chacha20-poly1305, ed25519, curve25519, ECDSA,
// ML-KEM, BLS, Diffie-Hellman, HKDF, PBKDF2, Argon2, Merkle trees, and
// the constant-time primitive surface.
//
// Fix: created ooda/std/crypto/mod.oo as the single public entry door.
// The mod.oo imports the public-API siblings and re-exports them with
// a stable crypto_mod_* prefix to avoid name collisions with the
// private internal siblings (cores, stubs, invariants, theory,
// principle, kat).
//
// Public API surface (11 functions re-exported):
//   crypto_mod_hash_sha256
//   crypto_mod_hash_hmac_sha256
//   crypto_mod_sym_aes_encrypt
//   crypto_mod_sym_aes_decrypt
//   crypto_mod_sym_chacha20_encrypt
//   crypto_mod_sym_chacha20_decrypt
//   crypto_mod_asy_ed25519_sign_hex
//   crypto_mod_asy_ed25519_verify_hex
//   crypto_mod_asy_curve25519_diffie_hellman
//   crypto_mod_kdf_hkdf
//   crypto_mod_kdf_pbkdf2
//
// Private siblings documented (do not import directly):
//   _core files: chacha20_core.oo, blake3_pure_core.oo, poly1305_core.oo
//   _stubs files: fhe_stubs.oo, keys_stubs.oo, attestation_stubs.oo
//   _invariants files: crypto_invariants.oo
//   _theory files: ml_kem_theory.oo, bls_signature_aggregation_law.oo
//   _principle files: constant_time_principle.oo, diffie_hellman_principle.oo
//   _kat files: crypto_kat.oo
//   _inv, _types, _store internal helpers
//
// Empirical verification: ooda/qa/tests_sovereign/tier1_features/test_t1_f22_crypto_mod_seam.oo
//   (15 assertions, 5 beats, 11 surface functions verified) is in the
//   working tree and parses/type-checks under ooda run.
//
// The mod.oo compiles cleanly under ooda check: "OK".

# === Beat 5: Audit verdict and path forward ===

// First-principles design (E-M / 80-20 / blue ocean):
//   Thrust -- the crypto/mod.oo fix closes the Pillar 6 seam violation
//     for the most security-critical subdirectory in one move. 80/20:
//     1 file (~100 lines) closes the violation for 61 internal files.
//   Drag -- none added. mod.oo is pure re-export; no new allocations,
//     no new subshells, no new process invocations.
//   Weight -- net +116 lines (mod.oo) +128 lines (test) = +244 lines
//     for the seam. 34 subdirectories still lack mod.oo.
//   Velocity -- unchanged for external callers (the re-exports are
//     trivial wrapper functions). Internal callers continue to be
//     importable directly; the mod.oo is a new entry point, not a
//     replacement.
//
// Path forward for the remaining subdirectories: 5-15 most-used public
// functions per subdir, mod.oo with re-export pattern (see crypto/),
// tier1 seam test (test_t1_f22_<subdir>_mod_seam.oo), audit TLDR update.
//
// This is a mechanical but large refactor (~340 lines of mod.oo
// + ~150 lines per test, x 34 subdirectories = ~17,000 lines). Out
// of scope for this audit pass; the crypto/ fix is the representative
// proof-of-concept.
//
// Progress: Batches 1+2+3 (Sept 1 2026) closed 14 of 34 subdirectories
// (5 new mod.oo + 4 stub upgrades + 5 new). See Beats 6+7+8.

# === Beat 6: Batch 1 Pillar 6 closure progress (Sept 1 2026) ===

// Five high-leverage subdirectories closed in Batch 1, following the
// representative crypto/mod.oo pattern. Each new mod.oo re-exports a
// stable <subdir>_mod_* surface and is verified by a tier1 seam test.
//
// Batch 1 deliverables (10 files, 976 lines aggregate, 80 re-exports):
//   core/mod.oo         68 lines / 24 re-exports   | hash/mod.oo        69 lines / 15
//   math/mod.oo         58 lines / 15 re-exports   | io/mod.oo          59 lines / 10
//   collections/mod.oo  62 lines / 16 re-exports   |
//   test_t1_f22_core_mod_seam.oo        142 lines  | test_t1_f22_hash_mod_seam.oo       132 lines
//   test_t1_f22_math_mod_seam.oo        130 lines  | test_t1_f22_io_mod_seam.oo         123 lines
//   test_t1_f22_collections_mod_seam.oo  133 lines  |
//
// Surface categories: core_mod_* (Option 5, Result 5, List 4, Str 4,
// JSON 2, DomainCert 2, Hash 2), math_mod_* (Stats 4, BigInt 2, Complex 4,
// Matrix 2, Constants 3), hash_mod_* (SHA-2 2, SHA-3 2, Keccak 2, BLAKE3 1,
// Legacy 2, NonCrypto 6), io_mod_* (Reader 2, Writer 2, Cursor 1,
// MemStream 2, LineReader 1, Bit 2), collections_mod_* (Catalog 2, Vec 3,
// Queue 3, Stack 3, Deque 1, HashMap 3, HashSet 1).
//
// Verification: each test asserts 15-19 invariants (T1.F22.1-19) covering
// surface-length, prefix-stability, and triple-run referential transparency.
//
// Remaining work: Batches 5-7 close the remaining 14 (actor, archive,
// bio, chem, compile, compression, econ, formal_proofs, hw, markup,
// principles, proof_verifiers, robot, ui).

